  "review_note": "2026-10-12: templateCentral 5.15 to 6.0.4. Ported the harness qkit adopted in its 6.0.1 and 6.0.4 reviews by 3-way merge, keeping this repo's local lines: project-anchored hook commands with timeouts, clean-tree Stop skip, additionalContext typecheck feedback, the Skill matcher, the per-segment block-no-verify parser with cwd-aware branch detection, protect-files path resolution, a verifier that fails on an unreadable manifest, a wider commit-msg gate, fail-closed PR doc gates in CI. Removed post-tool-failure.sh. Not adopted: exec-form hooks, the gitleaks syntax changes, ci-gates.sh, hooks/local, Azure DevOps and OpenCode items. Reasoning is in the AGENTS.md entry of the same date. Hashes below were recomputed from the LF-normalised blobs. Harness built to match the AGENTS.md 'AI Harness' section that had described it since the qkit-seeded bootstrap but was never actually built. Hooks/skills match qkit's simpler pattern; git-hook layer (lefthook) matches loopkit's, since that's this plan's chosen baseline. CI gates (changelog, readme-freshness, coverage) added to match loopkit's real working jobs. Follow-up: added the missing .claude/hooks/* Claude-Code-hook script layer (previously inline `node -e` one-liners embedded in settings.json), and fixed lefthook.yml's format-lint command, which had no exclude list and would have reformatted/drifted those scripts on first commit; version marker bumped 5.7.0 -> 5.11.0 to match sibling repo loopkit's harness architecture, which this change brings paykit's Claude Code hook layer up to.",
